      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Identify the following surface: \n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{7}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}=1\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the equation of an ellipsoid centered at $O$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=1,\n$$\n\nand an ellipsoid centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-{x}_{0})^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-{y}_{0})^{2}}{{b}^{2}}+\\frac{(z-{z}_{0})^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=1,\n$$\n\nThus, our equation is an ellipsoid with the following parameters:\n\n$$\n({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(1,-2,0),\\,a=3,\\,b=\\sqrt{7},\\,c=2.\n$$",
